============================================================
 Python REGEX Module — Pattern Syntax (Third‑Party Library)
============================================================

GENERAL METACHARACTERS
----------------------
.        Any character except newline (or any char with DOTALL)
^        Start of string or line
$        End of string or line
|        Alternation
(...)    Capturing group
(?:...)  Non‑capturing group
(?P<name>...)   Named capturing group
(?P=name)       Backreference by name
\1, \2, ...     Backreference by number

ESCAPES
-------
\d       Digit
\D       Non-digit
\w       Word character
\W       Non-word character
\s       Whitespace
\S       Non-whitespace
\A       Start of string only
\Z       End of string only
\G       End of previous match
\Q...\E  Literal text (quote mode)

QUANTIFIERS
-----------
*        0 or more
+        1 or more
?        0 or 1
{m}      Exactly m
{m,n}    Between m and n
{m,}     m or more

POSSESSIVE QUANTIFIERS (regex‑only)
-----------------------------------
*+       Possessive star
++       Possessive plus
?+       Possessive question
{m,n}+   Possessive range

ATOMIC GROUPS (regex‑only)
--------------------------
(?>...)  Atomic (no backtracking inside)

LOOKAROUNDS
-----------
(?=...)      Positive lookahead
(?!...)      Negative lookahead
(?<=...)     Positive lookbehind (variable‑length allowed)
(?<!...)     Negative lookbehind (variable‑length allowed)

CONDITIONALS
------------
(?(id/name)yes|no)
(?(id/name)yes)

COMMENTS
--------
(?#...)      Inline comment
(?x)         VERBOSE mode (ignore whitespace)

FLAGS (INLINE)
--------------
(?i)         IGNORECASE
(?s)         DOTALL
(?m)         MULTILINE
(?x)         VERBOSE
(?u)         UNICODE
(?V1)        VERSION1 behavior (regex‑only)
(?f)         FULLCASE (regex‑only)


============================================================
 Python REGEX Module — Advanced Structural Syntax
============================================================

SUBROUTINES & RECURSION (The "Structural" Core)
----------------------------------------------
(?R)           Recurse the entire pattern
(?n)           Recurse the pattern of numbered group 'n'
(?-n)          Relative recursion (n-th previous group)
(?&name)       Subroutine call to a named group/definition
(?(DEFINE)...) Define a block of reusable sub-patterns

CHARACTER SET LOGIC (VERSION 1 - (?V1))
---------------------------------------
[[a-z]--[aei]] Set Subtraction (consonants: a-z minus vowels)
[[a-z]&&[p-z]] Set Intersection (only chars in both sets)
[[a-z]||[0-9]] Set Union (combination of sets)
[^...]         Negated Character Set (matches any char NOT listed)
[...]          Character set

FUZZY MATCHING (regex-only)
---------------------------
(?e)...        Enables fuzzy matching
(...){e<2}     Match with less than 2 errors (insert/delete/sub)
(...){s<2}     Match with less than 2 substitutions
(...){i<2}     Match with less than 2 insertions
(...){d<2}     Match with less than 2 deletions

ADVANCED BOUNDARIES
-------------------
\b             Word boundary (start/end of word)
\B             Non-word boundary
\K             Reset start of match (discards everything before \K)
\m             Start of word
\M             End of word
\h             Horizontal whitespace
\H             Non-horizontal whitespace
\v             Vertical whitespace
\V             Non-vertical whitespace

GROUPING MODIFIERS
------------------
(?>...)        Atomic Grouping (no backtracking; "locks" the match)
(?|...|...)    Branch Reset (groups in different branches share IDs)
(?<name>...)   Alternative syntax for (?P<name>...)

REPETITION & QUANTIFIERS
------------------------
*+             Possessive zero-or-more (does not give back)
++             Possessive one-or-more
?+             Possessive zero-or-one
{m,n}+         Possessive range
